howard:{"n":"Howard Baldwin","d":"c. 1845–1928 · Brisbane","x":1928,"s":"y","p":["howard0","elizabethbr"],"r":["uk","au"],"t":"Married Anna Haill in the Bosmere district of Suffolk in 1864 and brought his family out to Queensland. By the mid-1880s he was in business in Fortitude Valley, Brisbane, as a poultry and egg merchant, and later a wholesale poulterer, in Wickham Street; he advertised as far away as the Warwick Argus for country farmers to send him their fowls and fresh eggs by rail to the Brunswick Street station, promising \"prompt returns, highest prices, no expenses deducted\", and he regularly sued customers in the Small Debts Court for unpaid poultry bills. The family lived in Alfred Street, in the Valley, where their daughter Bessie died in August 1889.\n\nHe died in 1928, aged 83, and was buried in Toowong Cemetery on 9 March 1928. One of his sons was named Howard Bristo Baldwin, after Howard's mother's family.","src":[["Advertisement, Warwick Argus, 25 Feb 1890","https://trove.nla.gov.au/newspaper/article/76983311"],["Advertisement, Warwick Argus, 22 Nov 1890","https://trove.nla.gov.au/newspaper/article/76985372"],["Funeral of Bessie Baldwin, Brisbane Courier, 10 Aug 1889","https://trove.nla.gov.au/newspaper/article/3499795"],["Death of Howard Bristo Baldwin, Courier-Mail, 15 Jun 1949","https://trove.nla.gov.au/newspaper/article/49686427"]]},
annahaill:{"n":"Anna Haill","d":"c. 1846–1939 · Brisbane","x":1939,"s":"y","p":["williamhaill","annapawsey"],"r":["uk","au"],"t":"Married Howard Baldwin in Suffolk in 1864 and came with him to Queensland, where he became a poultry and egg merchant in Fortitude Valley, Brisbane. In August 1889 they buried their daughter Bessie from their home in Alfred Street, in the Valley. Anna outlived Howard by eleven years. She died on 30 September 1939 at Bayview Terrace, Eagle Junction, \"in her 94th year\", and is buried with him in Toowong Cemetery. Bayview Terrace was also the street of Ryecroft, the Warbrick home, where her great-grandson Bruce Brazier's wedding reception had been held in 1929.","src":[["Death notice, Courier-Mail, 2 Oct 1939","https://trove.nla.gov.au/newspaper/article/40898124"],["Funeral of Bessie Baldwin, Brisbane Courier, 10 Aug 1889","https://trove.nla.gov.au/newspaper/article/3499795"]]},
