aaldrikhes:{"n":"Aaldrik Andries Hes","d":"innkeeper and merchant, Sappemeer","s":"b","p":[],"r":["nl"],"t":"An innkeeper and merchant (herbergier, koopman) at Sappemeer. An inn on the Winschoterdiep was a place of business as much as a tavern: skippers, peat bosses and shipwrights made their bargains there, and the innkeeper commonly traded on his own account as well.\n\nOn 24 January 1771 he signed a marriage contract with Albertje Remmerts Niemeijer, a farmer's daughter from Scheemda, with his brother Lucas Andries Hes standing on his side, and they married at Sappemeer three days later. Their children were Bouwina (1771), Klaaske (about 1776) and Aaldrik Andries, baptised on 24 November 1782. The son went to sea as a sailor (matroos) and in 1812 married Jacoba van der Waals, a maid born in Leiden.","src":[["Marriage contract, 1771","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:411cb5c4-d2cb-79c4-5600-acc515b873e3"],["Marriage at Sappemeer, 1771","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:ad948f45-f6b6-0df5-b6d7-3d6fe005e0c7"],["Baptism of Aaldrik Andries, 1782","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:3105f588-8049-8262-68cd-78d7eb45c0d2"],["Marriage of Aaldrik Andries Hes, 1812","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:7b25b37b-43a1-6ec1-44c9-5258278fb44c"]]},
albertjen:{"n":"Albertje Remmerts Niemeijer","s":"b","p":["remmertn","bouchien"],"r":["nl"],"t":"Born at Scheemda about 1738, the daughter of the farmer Remmert Tjarks Niemeijer and Bouchien Alberts. She was past thirty when she married Aaldrik Andries Hes at Sappemeer on 27 January 1771, with a contract signed three days earlier; Bouke Alberts and Remke Tonkes stood on her side.\n\nShe kept the inn at Sappemeer with her husband and had Bouwina (1771), Klaaske (about 1776) and Aaldrik Andries (1782), the last when she was about 44. She outlived her daughter Klaaske, who died in 1821, and spent her last years in the city of Groningen, where she died on 4 May 1823, aged 85.","d":"c. 1738–1823 · Scheemda","b":1738,"x":1823,"src":[["Death record, 1823","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:6a3ec028-23af-e663-42d6-6bf6b82696e1"],["Marriage contract, 1771","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:411cb5c4-d2cb-79c4-5600-acc515b873e3"],["Death of Klaaske Aaldriks Hes, 1821","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:66ae49d6-8f57-f71d-a690-1fb294da5608"]]},
harmijzer:{"n":"Harm Jacobs IJzer","d":"day labourer","s":"b","p":[],"r":["nl"],"t":"A day labourer (dagloner) at Oudeschans, the little fortress built in 1593 to guard the road into Groningen from the east. By his time the garrison was small and the village lived from farm work on the surrounding polders.\n\nWith his wife Antje Jans he had children baptised in the fortress church: Dorothea in September 1754, Boele in March 1757 and Jochem in November 1759. An older son, Jacob Harms IJzer, born about 1750, lived all his life at Oudeschans and died there in 1818. The surname IJzer means iron. Stijntje Jacobs IJzer, who died in 1819, is recorded as his daughter, though she may have been his granddaughter.","src":[["Baptism of Dorothea, 1754","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:fb207b7a-aa09-cc27-928d-a3052dc169c8"],["Baptism of Boele, 1757","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:69afa3e9-120e-47bd-795e-3f3abaca69cc"],["Baptism of Jochem, 1759","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:d24e5123-13b8-a0af-f341-5b54cea467fe"],["Death of Jacob Harms IJzer, 1818","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:ec9b91e7-ef02-11dd-00aa-6a7c80860995"]]},
antjejans:{"n":"Antje Jans","s":"b","p":[],"r":["nl"],"t":"Wife of the day labourer Harm Jacobs IJzer of Oudeschans. Their children Dorothea (1754), Boele (1757) and Jochem (1759) were baptised in the church inside the fortress; Boele's name probably came from her side of the family, as her son Jacob's death record calls her Antje Boeles. She is named as the mother of Stijntje Jacobs IJzer in Stijntje's death record of 1819.","src":[["Baptism of Boele, 1757","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:69afa3e9-120e-47bd-795e-3f3abaca69cc"],["Death record of Stijntje, 1819","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:de197a07-af33-80b5-d0c4-c02a4d6ece07"]]},
