derkeh:{"n":"Derk Eppes Hekman","d":"c. 1756–1817 · Nieuwe Pekela","s":"b","p":[],"r":["nl"],"t":"A master carpenter (meester timmerman) at Nieuwe Pekela. The Pekela villages were peat colonies, strung for kilometres along a canal dug to carry the turf away, and by his day they were turning to shipping and shipbuilding, so there was steady work for a carpenter with his own business.\n\nHis children included Epke (about 1786), Kornelius (1787), Wija (about 1791), Eppe (1795), Bijke (about 1798) and Lammert (1801). Three sons followed him into the trade; Kornelius was already a \"carpenter-boss\" (timmerbaas) at 24. Nearly every record names his wife as Jantje Kornelis Bakker, though Epke's marriage record calls her mother Jantjen Egberts. He died at Nieuwe Pekela on 20 May 1817, aged 61. His son Eppe was found drowned in the canal at Winschoten, under the English Bridge, in October 1840.","src":[["Marriage, Midwolda, 1813","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:1bf7e209-2371-0998-5338-a71fa4a62084"],["Death record, 1817","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:f302ea09-cf73-24d1-8269-e35260f2b515"],["Marriage of Kornelius, 1812","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:714ab780-2aff-4981-affc-d01002d16372"],["Marriage of Eppe, 1816","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:dc75eae5-7bf8-c6d7-166f-695f585ad6ea"],["Death of Eppe, 1840","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:93a47251-106a-b0b5-f094-17429f348b4f"]],"b":1756,"x":1817},
jantjenegb:{"n":"Jantjen Egberts","s":"b","p":[],"r":["nl"],"t":"Named as the mother of Epke Derks Hekman when Epke married at Midwolda in 1813. In every other record of the family the wife of the Nieuwe Pekela carpenter Derk Eppes Hekman is Jantje Kornelis Bakker, the mother of Kornelius (1787), Wija, Eppe (1795), Bijke and Lammert (1801). Either Jantjen Egberts was an earlier wife who died soon after Epke's birth about 1786, or the clerk at Midwolda wrote the wrong second name and the two are one woman. The records found so far do not settle it.","src":[["Marriage, Midwolda, 1813","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:1bf7e209-2371-0998-5338-a71fa4a62084"],["Marriage of Kornelius, 1812","https://www.openarchieven.nl/gra:714ab780-2aff-4981-affc-d01002d16372"]]},
